  "_comment": [
    "#1538 — the reference seeded board for `coord web --fixture`.",
    "Covers one pipeline row per stage: work running (and past its #846",
    "wall-clock threshold, so the frozen `now` below is load-bearing), work",
    "failed, test failed, review approved, merge queued, and merged/done.",
    "Every timestamp is a fixed epoch offset from `now` — nothing here reads",
    "the wall clock, so two runs produce byte-identical /api/pipeline output.",
    "The `events` script below does NOT auto-play: subscribe to /events first,",
    "then POST /api/fixture/events/replay. Schema: coord/dashboard/fixture.py.",
    "",
    "#3026 — board.fleet_health seeds GET /api/machines/health with five rows",
    "spanning all four severities plus a stale row: precision=ok,",
    "dellserver=unknown (offline, matches its `machines` reachability entry",
    "below), gpu-box=warn, build-runner=crit, spare-mini=ok-but-stale (last",
    "measured OK a long time ago — the 'OK' vs 'last measured OK, a while",
    "ago' distinction #1630 exists for). Top-level `machine_metrics` seeds",
    "GET /api/machines/metrics: precision's series has a gap (no sample",
    "between now-90 and now-30 — e.g. a daemon restart, since the ring buffer",
    "is memory-only) and one 'unknown' sample sandwiched between real",
    "readings; dellserver's series is unknown end-to-end, matching its",
    "offline reachability entry."
  ],
